# Rust crates

- `ambar-automation` (engine: triggers, conditions, the closed action set, permissions), `ambar-service` (`ambard`: IPC with owner token, approvals, agents, audit log, systemd/launchd), `ambar-cli` (`ambar`), `ambar-ai` (draft automations from text via Anthropic/OpenAI/Ollama), `ambar-pkg` (signed packages).
- The action set is closed by design. Never add an action that runs a program, a shell command or arbitrary code, and never let AI output or a package widen it.
- Paths are confined to granted folders (symlink and `..` escapes are tested). Destructive actions (trash, overwrite) need approval.
- Agents must never reach owner-only operations; revocation must cut live connections.
- `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`, no new `unsafe`, MSRV 1.89, `--locked` everywhere.
- Security fixes come with a test that fails when the protection is removed (see the sabotage table in `docs/STATUS.md`).
- AI tests use mock servers; never require a real API key.
